<body>
    <h1>Send Email</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<p>The =E2=80=9CSend Email=E2=80=9D panel is a feature that allows you to s=
end an email according to the settings you configure.</p><span class=3D"con=
fluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manu=
al-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" width=3D"256=
" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"5eab1336bcf2ba82a85c929f12cc0872dfab52bad2c61df43=
4689fab2b4722e1" data-image-src=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki/dow=
nload/attachments/3424452641/Screenshot%202024-10-25%20at%202.27.00%E2%80%A=
FPM.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1729891665390&amp;cacheVersion=
=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"157" data-width=3D"540" data-unresolved-c=
omment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"4236673025" data-linked-resou=
rce-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-reso=
urce-default-alias=3D"Screenshot 2024-10-25 at 2.27.00=E2=80=AFPM.png" data=
-base-url=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-con=
tent-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"3424452641" da=
ta-linked-resource-container-version=3D"10" data-media-id=3D"52737b94-0055-=
4be8-91a5-c8ab96eeaf63" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"74"></span>
<h3 id=3D"SendEmail-Configuration">Configuration</h3>
<p>To use this feature, you need to specify the following settings:</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout two-equal" data-layout=3D"two-equal">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Set as Flow Initiator</strong>: By selecting "Set as Flow Initia=
tor," this panel will serve as the starting point of the IVR flow, before p=
roceeding to subsequent panels within the Logic+ flow.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Panel Name</strong>: It is recommended that you choose a name an=
d keep it consistent. You will also need to specify the variable name to up=
date. If the variable does not exist, it will be created.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Panel Description</strong>: It is recommended to provide a clear=
 description of the panel, detailing its purpose and functionality. This is=
 akin to documentation, making it easier for others to understand and ident=
ify its intended use when they encounter it.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>To Address</strong>: This is the email address or addresses wher=
e you want to send the email. If you want to use a variable, separate the e=
mail addresses with a comma.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>From Name</strong>: This is the name associated with the sender =
of the email.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>From Address</strong>: This is the email address of the sender.<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Subject</strong>: This is the subject of the email.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Body</strong>: This is the full text content of the email body. =
It supports HTML, so you can use formatting to make the email more visually=
 appealing.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Exit Paths:</strong> Use the dropdown menu to select another pan=
el in your flow. Any output from this panel will advance to the linked pane=
l.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Default:</strong> The Default path is taken upon panel execution=
.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error: </strong>The path taken when there is an error</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<p></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper=
 confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image i=
mage-center" width=3D"318" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"2c80d478a67b55517c42724c=
c25170239fa93d5faba8c13a0129f46080835706" data-image-src=3D"https://sharpen=
cx.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/3424452641/Screenshot%202024-10-=
29%20at%2010.10.15%E2%80%AFAM-20241029-171321.png?version=3D1&amp;modificat=
ionDate=3D1730222328315&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"5=
97" data-width=3D"198" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-reso=
urce-id=3D"4243947526" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resou=
rce-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"Screenshot 20=
24-10-29 at 10.10.15=E2=80=AFAM-20241029-171321.png" data-base-url=3D"https=
://sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image=
/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"3424452641" data-linked-resource=
-container-version=3D"10" data-media-id=3D"b84fd939-b480-4978-bfe0-30faf2d4=
7cde" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"957"></span>
<p></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>To create tailored emails that apply directly to the recipient, use inte=
raction variables. This is especially helpful for the email subject and bod=
y. By using interaction variables, you can create content that is specific =
to each recipient, making the email more personal and engaging.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>Related Article: <a href=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/=
CT1/pages/4231364609/Available+Predefined+Variables" data-linked-resource-i=
d=3D"4231364609" data-linked-resource-version=3D"18" data-linked-resource-t=
ype=3D"page">Available Predefined Variables</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
